coder › Implemented the token bucket in `src/limiter.ts`.

What changed
- `RateLimiter` now keeps `tokens` and `lastRefill` state.
- It starts full: `tokens = capacity`, `lastRefill = now()`.
- `available` refills up to the current time and returns the (possibly fractional) token count.
- `tryTake(n = 1)` refuses any `n > capacity` outright, refills to the current time, and only deducts if enough tokens are present.
- Refill is `elapsedMs * refillPerSecond / 1000`, capped at `capacity`.

Tests added in `src/limiter.test.ts`
- starts full
- takes exactly `n` and leaves the rest
- takes nothing when short
- `n > capacity` is always refused
- continuous fractional refill
- never refills past capacity

